return DecodeH323_UserInformation(buf, p, len, &q931->UUIE);
Reason:
When len is zero, the decrement causes an integer underflow to -1, which is interpreted as a large unsigned positive value when passed to DecodeH323_UserInformation, leading to an out-of-bounds read. No bounds check was performed on len after the decrement.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
p++;
len--;
if (len <= 0)
    break;
return DecodeH323_UserInformation(buf, p, len, &q931->UUIE);
Reason:
The added check ensures that after decrementing len by 1 to skip the protocol discriminator byte, len is positive. If len is zero or negative (due to underflow), the code breaks out of the loop instead of passing an invalid length to the decoder, thus preventing the out-of-bounds read.

